.TH SLCTL 1 "2025-04-05" "SparkLink" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slctl \- SparkLink device control utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slctl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slctl
is an interactive command\-line tool for controlling SparkLink wireless
devices. It communicates with the
.BR slkd (8)
daemon over D\-Bus.
.PP
When invoked without arguments,
.B slctl
enters an interactive shell with a
.B [slk]#
prompt. Command history is saved to
.IR ~/.slctl_history .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage and commands without connecting to D\-Bus.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show the version without connecting to D\-Bus.
.TP
.B \-\-session
Use the session bus for isolated tests. The system bus is the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-adapter " path"
Select a live adapter registration for a one\-shot command. A command is required.
For example, use the path returned by
.B list
with
.B scan on
or
.BR "advertise on" .
.SH SUPPORT BOUNDARY
This unreleased CLI retains legacy command spellings. Pair/security, legacy
services/remote-services/read/write, PHY setters, RAL/RPA, sync, measurement,
PM and extended-advertising commands are not qualified Native capabilities
and may explicitly fail NotSupported. Their descriptions below name the
historical operation, not an implementation promise. Current SSAP operations
use the distinct ssap-* commands and canonical Connection objects. Consult
project/current-capabilities.md for exact source/artifact qualifications.
All experimental driver and real WS73 operations remain VM-only.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Discovery and Connection
.TP
.B list
List available adapters.
.TP
.B show
Show adapter information and status.
.TP
.B scan on|off
Start or stop device scanning.
.TP
.B devices
List discovered devices.
.TP
.BI info " address"
Show detailed information for a device.
.TP
.BI pair " address"
Legacy pairing facade; currently NotSupported.
.TP
.BI connect " address"
Connect to a device.
.TP
.BI disconnect " [address]"
Disconnect the current or specified device.
.SS Explicit Reference Security
.TP
.B agent
Run one foreground, explicit human Agent for the selected controller. Only
sdk111-no-mitm is supported; there is no automatic approval. Enter approve or
reject followed by the exact current request id before its original deadline.
Quit, EOF and Ctrl-C unregister only this Agent, without stopping the controller.
A pollable terminal or pipe is required; input lines are limited to 512 bytes.
.TP
.BI security-request " connection-path [timeout-ms]"
Allocate, begin and observe one author-owned request on the same bus connection.
Timeout is 1 through 5000 milliseconds, default 5000, including policy waiting;
approval never renews it. Start the passive T request before active G, with
explicit Agents on both controllers. Ctrl-C only attempts this request's cancel.
Both commands pin the original daemon owner and canonical connection identity.
These experimental commands require management/Agent permission, not just an
application channel grant. Exact CLI real-device qualifications are listed in project/current-capabilities.md;
they do not imply complete security or deployment support.
.PP
Success only reports the limited unauthenticated SDK111 reference mechanism,
not authenticated peer identity, a trusted Grant, Bond or application delivery.
Rejection, timeout, ownership loss and incomplete native results exit nonzero.
Legacy Pair/Encrypt do not invoke this workflow.
.SS SSAP Services
.TP
.B services
Legacy facade; currently NotSupported. Use the distinct local SSAP API.
.TP
.B remote\-services
Legacy facade; currently NotSupported. Remote SSAP uses a Connection actor.
.TP
.BI read " handle"
Legacy facade; currently NotSupported.
.TP
.BI write " handle hex_data"
Legacy facade; currently NotSupported.
.SS PHY and Radio Control
.TP
.BI role " [g|t]"
Get or set role (GL or T).
.TP
.B phy
Show current PHY parameters.
.TP
.BI mcs " index"
Set MCS (modulation/coding scheme) index.
.TP
.BI txpower " dBm"
Set transmit power in dBm.
.TP
.BI bandwidth " MHz"
Show or set channel bandwidth.
.SS Adaptive Frequency Hopping
.TP
.B afh get
Get current AFH channel map.
.TP
.BI afh " set hex_map"
Set AFH channel map.
.TP
.BI afh " hop handle"
Trigger a frequency hop on a connection.
.SS Resolving Address List
.TP
.B ral size
Show RAL capacity and usage.
.TP
.B ral clear
Clear the resolving address list.
.TP
.BI ral " add irk_hex addr_hex"
Add an entry to the RAL.
.TP
.BI ral " remove addr_hex"
Remove an entry from the RAL.
.SS Resolvable Private Address
.TP
.B rpa on|off
Enable or disable RPA generation.
.TP
.BI rpa " timeout seconds"
Set RPA rotation timeout.
.SS Sync Links
.TP
.BI sync " info id"
Show sync link information.
.TP
.BI sync " ucast\-rm id"
Remove a unicast sync link.
.TP
.BI sync " mcast\-rm id"
Remove a multicast sync link.
.SS Peer Information
.TP
.BI peer " features handle"
Query supported features of a connected peer.
.TP
.BI peer " version handle"
Query version information of a connected peer.
.SS Measurement
.TP
.B meas cap
Show measurement capabilities.
.TP
.B meas on
Enable measurement reporting.
.TP
.B meas off
Disable measurement reporting.
.SS Extended Advertising
.TP
.BI extadv " enable handle"
Enable an extended advertising instance.
.TP
.BI extadv " disable handle"
Disable an extended advertising instance.
.TP
.BI extadv " remove handle"
Remove an extended advertising instance.
.TP
.BI extadv " info handle"
Get extended advertising instance information.
.SS Statistics and Diagnostics
.TP
.B power
Show power management status.
.TP
.B dli
Show data\-link indicator information.
.TP
.B stats
Show the native LinkSnapshot summary; not mixed legacy subsystem counters.
.TP
.B events
Show the selected registration event position; not delivered/ACK/pending counts.
.TP
.B mgmt
Show management statistics.
.SS Interactive Shell
.TP
.B help
Print the list of available commands.
.TP
.B quit\fR,\fP exit
Exit the interactive shell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS
Override the system bus address for D\-Bus communication.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.slctl_history
Interactive shell command history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error communicating with slkd or invalid command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slkd (8),
.BR sparklink.conf (5)
